### Tone: End-of-game award: Pessimist, the player who guessed too low most often (at least three times, two answers in
### three). $count: those answers. The world is bigger than they think; dry, mock-sympathetic.

award-pessimist-1 =
    The Pessimist award goes to { $name }: too low { $count ->
        [one] once.
       *[other] { $count } times.
    } The world is bigger than you think. Much bigger. I’m sorry.
award-pessimist-2 = { $name }, you underestimate everything. A cautious approach. A wrong one, but cautious.
award-pessimist-3 = Pessimist: { $name }. In your universe, everything is small, short and rare. It sounds tidy. It isn’t ours.
award-pessimist-4 = { $name } aimed low, every time. The truth kept going up. You kept not following it.
award-pessimist-5 =
    { $count ->
        [one] One answer
       *[other] { $count } answers
    } too low from { $name }. Your glass is not half empty. It’s a thimble.
award-pessimist-6 = The award for modest expectations goes to { $name }. Modest, and then a bit more modest.
award-pessimist-7 = Pessimist: { $name }. Please never estimate how much food to bring to a party.
award-pessimist-8 = { $name }, consistently too low. Reality has more of everything than you planned for.
award-pessimist-9 = The Pessimist goes to { $name }, who looks at the world through the wrong end of the telescope.
award-pessimist-10 = { $name }, the most careful estimator here. So careful, the answers kept escaping above you.
award-pessimist-11 = { $name } guessed too low { $count } times. You expected less of the world. The world over-delivered.
award-pessimist-12 = Pessimist: { $name }. The glass is not half empty. In your estimate, it is a thimble.
award-pessimist-13 = The Pessimist goes to { $name }. Low expectations, consistently met. By you. Not by reality.
award-pessimist-14 = { $name }, too low, again and again. Reality kept being more. You kept being surprised.
award-pessimist-15 = Pessimist: { $name }. You rounded the universe down. It refused.
